anna: Heads up — ran into a weird edge with streaming + auth refresh on the Electron quickstart. When the token refresh happens mid-stream the client sometimes throws `Unexpected end of JSON input`.

anna: Repro: start a long generation, let auth refresh trigger (short TTL test token). Sometimes the client reconnects and the replayed chunk sequence merges wrong order and we end up parsing a truncated JSON object.

josh: Is this only Electron? Browser fetch streams handle partial chunks differently iirc.

anna: So far reproducible on Electron (macOS and Windows in VM). Chrome tab using same quickstart doesn't fail. Node SDK seems to behave differently too — it resumes fine in our CI.

priya: Possible reasons: (1) our Electron sample uses a polyfill that emits chunks as lines and treats each chunk as an event; (2) when auth refresh inserts its own small chunk ("\n" or a heartbeat) the client code tries to JSON.parse the intermediate buffer; (3) TextDecoder streaming differences across runtimes.

alex: We saw similar in a customer bug where reconnect+retry logic replayed buffered KV cache and duplicated a partial event. Could be retry idempotency bug.

infra-bot: ci/build 2026-04-02T09:40:20Z: sampleapp-electron (matrix: win-latest, mac-latest) queued.

josh: Quick diagnostic: can you capture raw byte sequence (hex) around the failure? That will show whether we lost bytes or mis-ordered.

anna: Pasted sample of failing stream (simplified):
```
// chunk A
{"id":1,"choices":[{"delta":{"content":"This is a lo"}}]}
// chunk B (arrives after reconnect)
{"choices":[{"delta":{"content":"ng sentence."}}]}
```
Client saw chunk A alone and attempted parse -> fine. But in some runs chunk A was cut at "lo and next chunk started with "ng... so first parse failed.

priya: That indicates we attempted to parse on chunk boundary. We should never parse until we've confirmed the SSE event delimiter (\n\n) and reassemble correctly. Also normalize CRLF.

alex: For parity we should add a single sse-stream util in node-sdk/browser-sdk that: does TextDecoder streaming safely, normalizes CRLF, accumulates until delimiter, and exposes an async iterator of parsed JSON events. Then sampleapps use that instead of ad-hoc handlers.

josh: Agree. Also add a small opt-in resume token check so retries don't double-apply partial events. For reconnect logic: when connection resumes, check the last server-sent sequence id and drop any new events <= last processed id.

infra-bot: issue created: SDK-2873 (sse-streaming-resume-and-parity).

anna: Minimal shim I tested locally in Electron (pseudo):
```
let dec = new TextDecoder();
let buf = '';
reader.read().then(function process({done, value}) {
  if (done) { if (buf.trim()) handle(buf); return; }
  buf += dec.decode(value, {stream: true});
  buf = buf.replace(/\r\n/g,'\n');
  const parts = buf.split('\n\n');
  buf = parts.pop();
  parts.forEach(p => {
    if (!p.trim()) return;
    try { handle(JSON.parse(p)); }
    catch(e) { /* keep for next chunk */ buf = p + buf; }
  });
  return reader.read().then(process);
});
```
This avoids JSON.parse on partial JSON and recovers when a partial chunk is later completed.

priya: Nice. Add tests: (a) chunk split in middle of multi-byte UTF-8 emoji, (b) chunk split in middle of an escaped unicode sequence, (c) auth refresh injects tiny chunk between bytes. Run these on win/mac/ubuntu matrix.

josh: We should also audit our Electron quickstart to ensure it doesn't use an EventSource polyfill that behaves differently. If we standardize on the SDK helper, quickstarts become thin wrappers.

anna: Created PRs — quickstart fix: https://git.internal/redwood/sampleapp/pull/1532 and SDK util: https://git.internal/redwood/node-sdk/pull/621. Both include tests and a short doc note in devex README about robust SSE handling.

alex: After the SDK util lands, let's bump sampleapp dependency and backport to previous quickstart versions. Also include a migration note for customers who used custom SSE handling.

priya: One more: add a small telemetry counter when we detect a mid-stream auth refresh so we can measure incidence in production (no PII).

infra-bot: label added: area/devex, priority/high

anna: I'll follow up with a short postmortem/summary when PRs merge and CI runs green. Thanks all! :tada:
